==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|la|Verulamium}}, the name of the [[Roman]] settlement on the same site.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} {{place|en|town|p/Britannia|c/Roman Empire}}. An ancient town in [[Roman Britain]], sited in the southwest of the modern city of [[St Albans]] in [[Hertfordshire]], [[England]], [[UK]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1905|author=w:Henrietta Elizabeth Marshall| title=w:Our Island Story| page=26|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/islandstorychild00mars/page/26/| passage=The first Christian martyr in Britain was called Alban. He lived in the town called '''Verulamium'''.}}

